---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---
<BaseLayout title="Material Procurement & Planning" description="A long-range material planning system combining inventory, open customer demand, scheduled receipts, historical consumption, and supplier lead times into purchasing recommendations.">

<section class="case-hero">
  <div class="container">
    <a class="case-back" href={`${base}/built-systems/`}>← Built Systems</a>
    <div class="case-kicker">07 / Procurement Planning</div>
    <h1>Material Procurement &<br/><em>Planning</em></h1>
    <p class="case-deck">A long-range planning system that combines current inventory, open customer demand, scheduled receipts, historical consumption, and supplier lead times to show what material is needed, how much to buy, and when to act.</p>
    <div class="case-role-line"><span>Demand Planning</span><span>Procurement</span><span>Forecasting</span><span>Data Integration</span><span>Decision Support</span></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="case-metrics case-metrics-dark">
  <div class="container case-metric-grid">
    <div><strong>~$3M</strong><span>Material Inventory Scope</span></div>
    <div><strong>18 Months</strong><span>Planning Horizon</span></div>
    <div><strong>20</strong><span>Materials in Portfolio Demo</span></div>
    <div><strong>Weekly</strong><span>Input Update Cycle</span></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="case-section">
  <div class="container case-two-col">
    <div>
      <div class="case-section-no">01</div><div class="eyebrow">The Planning Problem</div>
      <h2>Long lead times made a current inventory snapshot insufficient.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="case-copy">
      <p>Material purchasing required decisions months before the need reached production. Inventory, purchase orders, customer demand, and consumption history lived in separate sources.</p>
      <p class="case-emphasis">The model brings those signals together to show when coverage becomes tight, what needs to be ordered, and when purchasing should act.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="case-section case-alt section-divider material-input-section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="case-section-no">02</div><div class="eyebrow">Planning Model</div>
    <h2>Five inputs become one purchasing view.</h2>
    <div class="input-pipeline">
      <div><small>01</small><strong>Inventory</strong><span>On hand</span></div>
      <div><small>02</small><strong>Customer Demand</strong><span>Need dates</span></div>
      <div><small>03</small><strong>Open Orders</strong><span>Scheduled receipts</span></div>
      <div><small>04</small><strong>Consumption</strong><span>Historical baseline</span></div>
      <div><small>05</small><strong>Supplier Rules</strong><span>Lead time + constraints</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="pipeline-output">
      <span>DEMAND + COVERAGE MODEL</span><b>→</b><strong>Risk timing</strong><b>·</b><strong>Order quantity</strong><b>·</b><strong>Purchase date</strong>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="case-section material-demo-section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="case-section-no">03</div><div class="eyebrow">Portfolio Demo</div>
    <h2>A decision center for immediate purchasing and long-range coverage.</h2>
    <p class="case-intro">The downloadable workbook uses synthetic material, demand, purchasing, and transaction data. The Planning Hub consolidates the model into a single operating view.</p>

    <div class="material-demo-window">
      <div class="material-demo-bar"><span></span><span></span><span></span><b>Material Planning Hub</b></div>
      <div class="material-demo-body">
        <div class="material-demo-title"><small>DECISION CENTER</small><strong>Immediate orders, customer demand, and 18-month outlook</strong></div>
        <div class="material-kpis">
          <div><span>Materials Covered</span><strong>7</strong></div>
          <div><span>Immediate / Expedite</span><strong>5</strong></div>
          <div><span>Order Within 30 Days</span><strong>0</strong></div>
          <div><span>Suggested New Orders</span><strong>77K lb</strong></div>
        </div>
        <div class="material-action-table">
          <div class="material-table-head"><span>Material</span><span>Status</span><span>Suggested Order</span><span>Current Inventory</span><span>Open Orders</span><span>18M Forecast</span><span>Confidence</span></div>
          <div class="material-table-row"><span>MTL-004</span><em>EXPEDITE / ORDER NOW</em><span>21.8K lb</span><span>46.5K</span><span>19K</span><span>344K</span><b>48</b></div>
          <div class="material-table-row"><span>MTL-008</span><em>EXPEDITE / ORDER NOW</em><span>22.9K lb</span><span>9.4K</span><span>6K</span><span>73.9K</span><b>59</b></div>
          <div class="material-table-row"><span>MTL-003</span><i>MONITOR</i><span>—</span><span>12.8K</span><span>10K</span><span>34.1K</span><b>89</b></div>
          <div class="material-table-row"><span>MTL-010</span><strong>COVERED</strong><span>—</span><span>7.6K</span><span>32K</span><span>23.9K</span><b>88</b></div>
        </div>
        <div class="material-insight-strip">
          <div><span>Immediate purchasing exposure</span><strong>~77,026 lb across 5 materials</strong></div>
          <div><span>Estimated demo spend</span><strong>~$2.07M in suggested orders</strong></div>
          <div><span>Forecast confidence</span><strong>12 high · 4 medium · 4 low</strong></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="case-note">All quantities, costs, material IDs, and purchasing recommendations shown in the portfolio demo are synthetic.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="case-section case-alt material-demand-section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="case-section-no">04</div><div class="eyebrow">Demand Forecast</div>
    <h2>Compare what history suggests with what customers are already asking for.</h2>
    <div class="demand-visual">
      <div class="demand-chart-head"><strong>18-Month Demand Support</strong><span>Illustrative portfolio view</span></div>
      <div class="demand-chart">
        <div class="demand-y"><span>30K</span><span>20K</span><span>10K</span><span>0</span></div>
        <div class="demand-plot">
          <div class="quarter q1">Q1</div><div class="quarter q2">Q2</div><div class="quarter q3">Q3</div><div class="quarter q4">Q4</div><div class="quarter q5">Q5</div><div class="quarter q6">Q6</div>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 720 220" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true">
            <polyline class="hist-line" points="20,145 140,125 260,137 380,102 500,116 700,86"/>
            <polyline class="open-line" points="20,170 140,108 260,151 380,78 500,142 700,126"/>
            <polyline class="plan-line" points="20,145 140,108 260,137 380,78 500,116 700,86"/>
          </svg>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="demand-legend"><span><i class="hist"></i>Historical baseline</span><span><i class="open"></i>Visible customer demand</span><span><i class="plan"></i>Planning forecast</span></div>
      <div class="demand-rule"><span>For each planning period</span><strong>Use the stronger demand signal</strong><span>Past-due open demand rolls into the first period</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="case-section material-calendar-section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="case-section-no">05</div><div class="eyebrow">Purchasing Calendar</div>
    <h2>Translate the forecast into a weekly buying timeline.</h2>
    <div class="purchase-calendar-demo">
      <div class="calendar-legend"><span><i class="scheduled"></i>Scheduled receipt</span><span><i class="suggested"></i>Suggested order</span></div>
      <div class="calendar-grid">
        <div class="calendar-head"><span>Material</span><span>Jul</span><span>Aug</span><span>Sep</span><span>Oct</span><span>Nov</span><span>Dec</span><span>Jan</span><span>Feb</span></div>
        <div class="calendar-row"><strong>MTL-004</strong><span class="suggested">21.8K</span><span></span><span class="scheduled">8K</span><span></span><span></span><span class="scheduled">5K</span><span></span><span></span></div>
        <div class="calendar-row"><strong>MTL-007</strong><span></span><span class="suggested">8.2K</span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>
        <div class="calendar-row"><strong>MTL-008</strong><span class="suggested">22.9K</span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span class="scheduled">20K</span><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>
        <div class="calendar-row"><strong>MTL-010</strong><span></span><span class="scheduled">6K</span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span class="scheduled">10K</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="case-note">The workbook includes a rolling 52-week calendar that places scheduled receipts and recommended orders on the same timeline.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="case-section case-alt material-horizon-section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="case-section-no">06</div><div class="eyebrow">Long-Range Coverage</div>
    <h2>See where material coverage begins to tighten across the planning horizon.</h2>
    <div class="coverage-window">
      <div class="coverage-head"><strong>18-Month Material Outlook</strong><span>Inventory + receipts against forecast demand</span></div>
      <div class="coverage-grid">
        <div class="coverage-row coverage-labels"><span>Material</span><span>Q1</span><span>Q2</span><span>Q3</span><span>Q4</span><span>Q5</span><span>Q6</span><span>Action</span></div>
        <div class="coverage-row"><strong>MTL-004</strong><i class="ok">2.4×</i><i class="ok">1.7×</i><i class="watch">1.2×</i><i class="risk">0.8×</i><i class="risk">0.5×</i><i class="risk">0.3×</i><b>ORDER</b></div>
        <div class="coverage-row"><strong>MTL-008</strong><i class="watch">1.3×</i><i class="risk">0.9×</i><i class="risk">0.6×</i><i class="risk">0.4×</i><i class="risk">0.2×</i><i class="risk">0.1×</i><b>EXPEDITE</b></div>
        <div class="coverage-row"><strong>MTL-003</strong><i class="ok">3.1×</i><i class="ok">2.5×</i><i class="ok">1.9×</i><i class="watch">1.3×</i><i class="watch">1.1×</i><i class="risk">0.9×</i><em>MONITOR</em></div>
        <div class="coverage-row"><strong>MTL-010</strong><i class="ok">4.0×</i><i class="ok">3.5×</i><i class="ok">2.8×</i><i class="ok">2.2×</i><i class="ok">1.8×</i><i class="ok">1.5×</i><span>COVERED</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="coverage-legend"><span><i class="ok"></i>Covered</span><span><i class="watch"></i>Watch</span><span><i class="risk"></i>Risk</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="case-section material-ownership-section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="case-section-no">07</div><div class="eyebrow">Use & Handoff</div>
    <h2>A planning tool with visible assumptions and a clear review point.</h2>
    <div class="compact-governance">
      <div><strong>Procurement</strong><span>Updates receipts and reviews recommended orders.</span></div>
      <div><strong>Operations</strong><span>Maintains assumptions and reviews coverage risk.</span></div>
      <div><strong>Leadership</strong><span>Uses the outlook for spend and long-range exposure.</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="boundary-strip"><span>Safety stock</span><span>Lead time</span><span>Minimum buys</span><span>Yield loss</span><span>Shared supply</span><span>Forecast confidence</span></div>
    <p class="case-note">Recommendations remain planning outputs. Purchasing decisions still account for supplier constraints, changing production conditions, and planner judgment.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="case-section material-download">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="download-card">
      <div>
        <div class="eyebrow">Explore the Demo</div>
        <h2>Material Procurement & Planning Dashboard</h2>
        <p>Download the desktop Excel portfolio demo with synthetic inventory, customer demand, scheduled receipts, purchasing calendar, consumption review, planning recommendations, 12- and 18-month forecasts, operational insights, methodology, and instructions.</p>
      </div>
      <a href={`${base}/artifacts/material-procurement-planning-demo.xlsx`} download><span>Download Excel Demo</span><b>↓</b></a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="case-next">
  <div class="container">
    <span class="eyebrow">Related System</span>
    <a href={`${base}/built-systems/foundry-inventory/`}><strong>Production Supplies & Replenishment</strong><span>→</span></a>
  </div>
</section>
</BaseLayout>
